# A signed generic function that calls itself at a larger type than its own, `[a]` for
# `a` (Type System ch. 2: "Recursion at other indices needs the signature", so a signed
# function may call itself at other types, and no passage bounds them; ch. 5: a type
# variable is decided at each call). The program gives the function no finite set of
# types; how deep the run goes is the number it is given.
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

Depth: fn [a], Nat -> Nat
fn Depth xs, more = match more -? 1:
    ? less: Depth [[xs]], less
    nil: Len xs

@Page: @unit
@Page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Depth [[7, 8]], 2}")
